      {
        "test": "TC-TH-03",
        "text": "R10, Opening blocked when hot: two criteria failed. max_current_above_130C_a was 15.16 A against a limit of <= 15 A (13 samples above 15 A, first at t=39110 ms at 134.0 C, described as end-stop stalls). opening_starts_above_140C was 1 against a limit of 0: opening started at t=57050 ms at 143.9 C, and the controller completed full opening travel above 140 C with no inhibit. Not new: the opening-above-140 failure occurred on 10 of 10 nights under both v1.2 and v1.3, with limit 'no opening above 140' each night. Open defect DR-1012 (S3, Opening possible above 140 °C). The history covers only the opening-above-140 check. The fact sheet has no history for the 15 A current criterion, so it cannot be classed as new or repeated."
      }
